{
  "_doc": "FreeViewer test vectors for third-party viewers (OrientOS/Firn). TEST DATA ONLY - every secret below is public.\nAll binary values are lowercase hex strings. Generated and verified by src/vectors.rs (cargo test).\nSections:\n  primitives  : standard known-answer tests (RFC 7748 X25519, RFC 5869 HKDF-SHA256, RFC 4231 HMAC-SHA256, AES-256-GCM zero key).\n  handshake   : fixed viewer/host secrets + salt -> public keys, X25519 shared secret, session key, udp key, 4-digit code, handshake frames.\n                session_key = HKDF-SHA256(ikm = shared, salt = salt(16), info = 'freeviewer-v1 session') -> 32 bytes.\n                udp_key     = HKDF-SHA256(ikm = session_key, salt = none (zeros), info = 'freeviewer-v1 udp') -> 32 bytes.\n                session_code = SHA-256('freeviewer-v1 code' || session_key)[0..4] as u32 big endian, mod 10000, zero padded to 4 digits.\n                Frames: V->H 0x01||client_pub, H->V 0x02||host_pub||salt, V->H 0x03||proof, V->H 0x06||device_name(utf8), H->V 0x04 ok / 0x05 fail.\n  argon2      : password_key = Argon2id(password utf8, salt(16)), version 0x13, m=19456 KiB, t=2, p=1, no secret, no associated data, 32 byte output\n                (argon2 crate 0.5.3 Argon2::default()). proof = HMAC-SHA256(password_key, 'fv-auth' || client_pub || host_pub || salt). Uses client_pub/host_pub from 'handshake'.\n  cipher      : data frame = 0x10 || nonce(12) || AES-256-GCM(key = session_key, nonce, plaintext, no AAD) = ciphertext || tag(16).\n                nonce = direction byte (host->viewer = 1, viewer->host = 2) || 000000 || counter u64 big endian. Counter starts at 1 per direction, the receiver\n                rejects counter <= last accepted. plaintext_hex = proto encoding of the message named in 'msg'.\n  proto       : encode() bytes (hex) of every message type. Integers little endian; blobs/strings = u32 length + bytes. 'fields' is informative only.\n                dir: 'H->V' host sends, 'V->H' viewer sends, 'both'. Blob contents in this section are fake bytes (not real JPEG/H.264).\n  proto_reject: byte strings that decode() must reject (no crash, no message).\n  sample_jpeg : the real 16x16 JPEG used inside the cipher vectors Frame/Tiles (decodes to 16x16 RGB).\nLimits: max 4096 tiles per Tiles, max 8 MiB per Video, max 256 KiB clipboard text, max 512 KiB file chunk, max 32 monitors, max 64 resolutions.",
